nows there’s an attachment related to it. It’s all about clarity, so I want the user to easily understand that the image is connected to the information I’m providing! Let’s go ahead and shape that response.\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] **Kidney Cancer Detector**\nKidney cancer class: **kidney_tumor**\nConfidence: **99.99%**\nInference time: **3.27 seconds**\n\n**Image Analyzer**\nImage Analyzer prediction: **kidney_tumor**\nCAM coverage: **0.0128**\nCAM center ratio: **0.8250**\nCAM left-right asymmetry: **0.1000**\nCAM top-bottom asymmetry: **1.0000**\nCAM explanation: The model focused on a **localized central region within the kidney tissue**, with an asymmetric pattern that may fit a **localized structural abnormality**. A heatmap image is attached below for reference.\n\n**xAI**\nConfidence interpretation: The pipeline reports a **very high-confidence imaging signal**, but this still does **not** confirm a diagnosis on its own.\nSummary: The pipeline judged this scan as showing a **high likelihood of a kidney tumor signal**.\nVisual evidence: The analysis detected imaging features interpreted as a **kidney tumor pattern**.\n\n**Result Interpretation**\nThis result is **concerning**, especially because it lines up with the symptoms and history you already shared: **right flank pain, blood/pink urine, weight loss, fatigue, prior nephrectomy, and RCC follow-up history**. A musculoskeletal explanation alone would not fit the whole picture well. Even so, this pipeline is a **preliminary signal, not an actual diagnosis**, and it cannot replace clinician review, formal radiology interpretation, or confirm whether this is recurrence, a new lesion, or another kidney/urologic problem.\n\n**Recommendended next steps**\nBecause of both your symptoms and this imaging output, I would treat this as something to pursue **urgently** with your doctor / oncology-urology team. Ask for **prompt in-person assessment**, including formal imaging review and updated urine and blood testing. If you develop **heavy blood in urine, fever, vomiting, inability to urinate, severe worsening pain, faintness, or confusion**, go to the **ER immediately**.\n\nMEDIA:http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/admin/admin/retrieve-image-file/nodes_bucket/626130f7c71f6b9e651c76be/69b862e0a6fbd73a6254e5be/b0f1c107-0576-49f4-985a-1754b3411728.jpeg\n\nIf you want, I can now help you turn **our conversation plus this tool output** into a clearer patient-facing report using the **LLM Distillation** tool.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0ab7ac9648b5f8610169c78ec54b5c8191aaa656e6df299b61\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":10517,"output":554,"cacheRead":19200,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":30271,"cost":{"input":0.026292500000000003,"output":0.00831,"cacheRead":0.0048,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0394025}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774685889787}}
